00:45:41,660 --> 00:45:42,360
What happened?

531
00:45:43,040 --> 00:45:50,740
But I think it's interesting that the author points out three times in two chapters, Ruth is asked the question, who are you?

532
00:45:50,740 --> 00:45:56,540
And many people already assume they know who she is, based on where she comes from.

533
00:45:56,540 --> 00:46:05,040
But Ruth continually shows up and answers that question based on her character and a heart fully surrendered to God.

534
00:46:05,040 --> 00:46:10,240
So I think it would be helpful for us to ponder this question ourselves, who are we?

535
00:46:13,040 --> 00:46:18,680
Who are we really, both in the public square and in the secret place when nobody else is around?

536
00:46:18,680 --> 00:46:22,500
Who are we?

537
00:46:22,500 --> 00:46:27,960
Not what is the external identity markers that we've embraced.

538
00:46:27,960 --> 00:46:34,780
Not the beliefs and morals that we've intellectually agreed with.

539
00:46:34,780 --> 00:46:38,160
Not the religious hoops that we've jumped through.

540
00:46:38,160 --> 00:46:40,080
Who are we really?

541
00:46:40,940 --> 00:46:45,100
Jesus says, by your fruit, you will, by their fruit, you will recognize them.

542
00:46:45,100 --> 00:46:51,360
