543
00:46:51,360 --> 00:46:52,560
Who are we?

544
00:46:52,560 --> 00:46:59,260
Do our actions, both in the public square and in the secret place, line up with how we would intellectually answer that question?

545
00:46:59,260 --> 00:47:04,200
I think this is a worthy question for us to consider this week.

546
00:47:04,700 --> 00:47:05,260
Where are we?

547
00:47:05,260 --> 00:47:07,280
Where are the inconsistencies in our lives?

548
00:47:07,280 --> 00:47:12,960
What things do we need to bring into the light of God's grace to be forgiven and redeemed?

549
00:47:12,960 --> 00:47:15,040
Who are we?

550
00:47:15,040 --> 00:47:19,160
When no one else is around.

551
00:47:19,160 --> 00:47:23,440
When no one's going to find out who are we.

552
00:47:28,080 --> 00:47:38,420
May we not be a church filled with people who look really godly on Sunday mornings, but refuse to obey the principles of the kingdom of God all throughout the week.

553
00:47:38,420 --> 00:47:39,060
Who are we?

554
00:47:40,980 --> 00:47:44,940
Now, we've said throughout this series that the book of Ruth is the story of the whole Bible.

555
00:47:44,940 --> 00:47:53,100
We've talked a lot about the individual lives of Ruth, Naomi, and Boaz, but the reality is neither Ruth nor Boaz is the hero of this story.

556
00:47:53,100 --> 00:47:59,300
Yes, they pull up a chair beside the God that they have come to know and love, and yes, they say, I'm here to help.

557
00:47:59,300 --> 00:48:00,420
I want to participate.

558
00:48:00,420 --> 00:48:03,880
I want to receive your invitation to work out your redemption plan.

559
00:48:03,940 --> 00:48:07,360
But they, I'm sure, have their own cracked yokes on the ground.

560
00:48:07,360 --> 00:48:09,160
They have failed.

561
00:48:09,160 --> 00:48:09,860
They have fallen.

562
00:48:09,860 --> 00:48:11,400
They are not the heroes of the story.

563
00:48:11,400 --> 00:48:17,220
The reality is not only is this story about Ruth and Boaz, but this story is about you and I before a holy God.

564
00:48:17,220 --> 00:48:22,920
This story functions as a foreshadowing of the gospel.

565
00:48:22,920 --> 00:48:32,140
All of us are like Ruth, desperately in need of redemption, and Jesus has made that redemption available to us through his sacrificial life and death.

566
00:48:32,140 --> 00:48:34,860
So I don't ask you the question, who are you, to condemn you.

567
00:48:34,860 --> 00:48:49,480
I ask you the question, who are you, to invite you, to bring the true, honest, raw answer to Jesus Christ, who will redeem it, who will not condemn it, who will receive you with open arms, because he already knows the answer to that question.

568
00:48:49,480 --> 00:48:53,500
Whether or not you're willing to answer it honestly or not, he knows the answer to that question.

569
00:48:54,720 --> 00:49:04,200
And the invitation is for us to bring the answer to that question to him, knowing that we will not receive condemnation, but that we will see forgiveness, grace, and reconciliation.

